    "reason": "HALF OF THE PERIOD-1 CASE OF PRIZE 1, AND IT IS PROVABLE: the centre column is never white for good. Why it is true: at a white centre cell the rule at position 1 loses its xor term and becomes an OR, so column 1 at the next step is column 1 or column 2 at this one. If the centre column were white from N on, column 1 could therefore never turn from black back to white after N, so it is monotone, so it is eventually constant, so it is eventually periodic — and so is the centre column, with period 1. Two adjacent columns cannot both be eventually periodic (not_isEventuallyPeriodic_adjacent at i = 0). WHY AN OPEN NODE WOULD CITE IT: centerColumn_not_eventually_constant (open, size L) is LITERALLY the conjunction of this node and centerColumn_white_infinitely_often, in that order — it closes as one anonymous constructor once both land. PROVED IN SCRATCH with a self-contained route needing no other node of this tier: explorer/seeder_scratch_p1e.lean, axioms propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.",
    "disclaims": "Nothing above period 1. There is no induction on the period here and none is available: this half turns on a monotonicity that exists only when the centre column is white at EVERY late time, and one black cell in a period destroys it. So it is not a step toward either P1 wall, and the tier does not pretend it is. A mathematician would call this easy and would very likely call it folklore; it is not in any source held here, but I did not search the literature and it should not be reported as novel. The witness is a genuine instance check rather than a shadow — every N below 8 really does get a black cell below 12 — but it says nothing about large N, where the whole claim lives.",
    "route": {
      "tactics": "by_contra hcon\n  push_neg at hcon\n  have hN : ∀ t ≥ N, centerColumn t = false := by\n    intro t ht\n    have := hcon t ht\n    cases hx : centerColumn t with\n    | false => rfl\n    | true => exact absurd hx this\n  have mono : ∀ t, N ≤ t → evolve t 1 = true → evolve (t + 1) 1 = true := by\n    intro t ht hb\n    have e : evolve (t + 1) 1 = (evolve t 1 || evolve t 2) := by\n      rw [evolve_succ, rule30_eq]\n      norm_num\n      rw [show evolve t 0 = false from hN t ht]\n      simp\n    rw [e, hb]; rfl\n  have key : ∃ M, N ≤ M ∧ ∀ n ≥ M, evolve (n + 1) 1 = evolve n 1 := by\n    by_cases hex : ∃ t, N ≤ t ∧ evolve t 1 = true\n    · obtain ⟨t0, ht0, hb⟩ := hex\n      refine ⟨t0, ht0, ?_⟩\n      have all : ∀ s, evolve (t0 + s) 1 = true := by\n        intro s\n        induction s with\n        | zero => simpa using hb\n        | succ k ih =>\n            have := mono (t0 + k) (by omega) ih\n            rw [show t0 + (k + 1) = t0 + k + 1 by ring]\n            exact this\n      intro n hn\n      have e1 : evolve (n + 1) 1 = true := by\n        rw [show n + 1 = t0 + (n + 1 - t0) by omega]; exact all _\n      have e2 : evolve n 1 = true := by\n        rw [show n = t0 + (n - t0) by omega]; exact all _\n      rw [e1, e2]\n    · push_neg at hex\n      refine ⟨N, le_refl _, ?_⟩\n      intro n hn\n      have e1 : evolve (n + 1) 1 = false := Bool.not_eq_true _ |>.mp (hex (n + 1) (by omega))\n      have e2 : evolve n 1 = false := Bool.not_eq_true _ |>.mp (hex n (by omega))\n      rw [e1, e2]\n  obtain ⟨M, hNM, hcol1⟩ := key\n  refine not_isEventuallyPeriodic_adjacent 0 ⟨⟨1, one_pos, M, ?_⟩, ⟨1, one_pos, M, ?_⟩⟩\n  · intro n hn\n    show centerColumn (n + 1) = centerColumn n\n    rw [hN (n + 1) (by omega), hN n (by omega)]\n  · intro n hn\n    show evolve (n + 1) ((0 : ℤ) + 1) = evolve n ((0 : ℤ) + 1)\n    rw [show (0 : ℤ) + 1 = 1 by ring]\n    exact hcol1 n hn",
      "imports": ["Rule30.Prize", "Rule30.Proofs.NotIsEventuallyPeriodicAdjacent"]
    },
