    "id": "column_neg_two_damage_derivative",
    "lean_name": "column_neg_two_damage_derivative",
    "statement": "theorem column_neg_two_damage_derivative (X Y : Config) (t : ℕ)\n    (h0 : column X 0 t = column Y 0 t)\n    (h1 : column X 0 (t + 1) = column Y 0 (t + 1)) :\n    xor (column X (-2) t) (column Y (-2) t)\n      = xor (xor (column X (-1) t) (column Y (-1) t))\n          (xor (column X (-1) (t + 1)) (column Y (-1) (t + 1))) := by\n  sorry",
    "under": "centerColumn_other_isEventuallyPeriodic_of_center",
    "reason": "One column further left than the mask law, and there the mask disappears: the disagreement at column -2 is the plain discrete derivative of the disagreement at column -1. No masking, no `&&` — this is the one place in the leftward cascade where the relation is linear.\n\nWHY IT IS TRUE. `sideways_inverse` at position -1 gives column X (-2) t = column X (-1) (t + 1) XOR (column X (-1) t || column X 0 t), and the same for Y. XOR the two. The bracket is (u || a) XOR (u' || a), where a is the shared origin cell by h0 and u, u' are the two column--1 cells: it is false when a is black and the column--1 disagreement when a is white. The two cases then join, and that is the whole trick: when a is black, `column_succ_of_black` applied to X and to Y (they share the origin cell at t by h0 and at t + 1 by h1) pins both column--1 cells to the complement of the same cell, so the column--1 disagreement is false there too. So in BOTH cases the bracket equals the column--1 disagreement at t, and the identity is the stated XOR of it with the one at t + 1.\n\nWHY A PROOF OF THE WALL WOULD CITE IT. Under a centre column repeating at lag p, it converts 'column -2 repeats at time t' into 'the column--1 mismatch is the same at t and t + 1'. So column -2 is eventually periodic exactly when the column--1 mismatch is eventually constant — and eventually constant means either eventually zero (column -1 repeats at lag p) or eventually one (column -1 repeats at lag 2p). Jen forbids both. That is a genuine structural fact about the assumed picture, in the same currency as the mask law and one column further in.",
    "disclaims": "The cascade does NOT continue, and this is the honest limit of the statement rather than a gap in it. The same claim one column further left — that the disagreement at -3 is the discrete derivative of the disagreement at -2 — is measured FALSE: 418 failures in 35,795 hypothesis hits over random configuration pairs (explorer/seeder_p1_damage.mjs). The reason is visible in the proof: at column -2 the second input to the `||` is still the shared origin column, and at -3 it is not. So a prover should not expect an induction here, and a seeder should not propose one.",
    "witness": {
      "expression": "(List.range 12).all (fun v => ([1, 2] : List ℤ).all (fun f =>\n  (List.range 9).all (fun t =>\n    !(decide (column (fun i => decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3)) 0 t\n        = column (fun i => xor (decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3))\n            (decide (i = f))) 0 t) &&\n      decide (column (fun i => decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3)) 0 (t + 1)\n        = column (fun i => xor (decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3))\n            (decide (i = f))) 0 (t + 1))) ||\n    decide (xor (column (fun i => decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3)) (-2) t)\n        (column (fun i => xor (decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3))\n            (decide (i = f))) (-2) t)\n      = xor (xor (column (fun i => decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3)) (-1) t)\n              (column (fun i => xor (decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3))\n                (decide (i = f))) (-1) t))\n          (xor (column (fun i => decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3)) (-1) (t + 1))\n              (column (fun i => xor (decide ((i * i * i + (v : ℤ) * i + 1) % 7 < 3))\n                (decide (i = f))) (-1) (t + 1)))))))",
      "imports": ["Rule30.Basic"],
      "range": "the same twelve noisy rows v < 12, flip f in {1, 2}, every t < 9. Evaluated true by `lake env lean` at seed time (explorer/seeder_p1_final.lean). Non-vacuity: the column--1 disagreement is nonzero at four (v, f, t) inside this range, so the right-hand side is not identically false here. Independently: 0 failures in 76,711 hypothesis hits over 400 random configuration pairs, 4,398 of them with a nonzero left-hand side (explorer/seeder_p1_damage.mjs)."
